  "question": {
    "text": "Which of the following expressions corresponds to simple harmonic motion along a straight line, where $\\mathrm{x}$ is the displacement and $\\mathrm{a}, \\mathrm{b}, \\mathrm{c}$ are positive constants?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "gHI29",
      "text": "\n$a+b x-c x^2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "qk1NH",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{bx}^2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "40G5Z",
      "text": "\n$a-b x+c x^2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "lvlcl",
      "text": "\n$-b x$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "In linear S.H.M., the restoring force acting on particle should always be proportional to the displacement of the particle and directed towards the equilibrium position. i.e., $\\mathrm{F} \\propto \\mathrm{x}$\nor $\\mathrm{F}=-\\mathrm{bx}$ where $\\mathrm{b}$ is a positive constant.",
    "image": null
  },
